Changes adapt the addon to the stable FancyNpcs 2.12.1 source base and
ModelEngine R4.1.1,
including model lifecycle, visibility, scale, interaction and persistence
integration, and preserve the BetterModel provider. The 1.3.0 addon update
adds smooth head tracking and layered ambient idle animations; the core
version and retained upstream NMS implementations are unchanged.

Validation target: Paper 1.21.11, Java 25, ModelEngine R4.1.1.
The FancyNpcs core retains upstream multi-version implementations. The
repository retains all 7 NPC and 7 packet NMS source modules, including 26.x.
See the matching release validation.json for build, unit-test and headless
runtime findings, including the exact scope of tracking/ambient checks.
26.x ModelEngine integration is not claimed as validated. This addon does
not support Folia.
Player clicks, resource-pack visuals and multi-player visibility remain
manual checks. See validation.json for the exact verification scope.

Optional upstreamNmsJar builds reuse 432 unchanged implementation classes
from the official MIT-licensed FancyNpcs 2.12.1 JAR. The extraction tool
tools/extract_upstream_nms.py and pinned upstream-release.json verify the
official input and preserve original class bytes. Core, APIs, loader and
plugin metadata are rebuilt from local source. Omitting this property
compiles all retained source modules. SOURCE_COMMIT preserves the source
baseline for no-.git archives; sourceCommitHash can explicitly override
generated build metadata.

ModelEngine and BetterModel are external dependencies used for compilation
and installed separately at runtime. Their JARs, licenses and rights are not
redistributed or granted by this repository or its release archives.
Bundled dependency license notices in built plugin JARs remain intact;
this NOTICE does not relicense those dependencies.
